There are 2 types of routing
a)Client side routing         b)server side routing

Server side routing is a way in which all our pages come from server.Suppose,you are going on another route like about,that about page will come from server.In old times,we use server side routing but now in react,we use client side routing.In client side routing,we not need to get data from server.

Imp Point 1:
we can use anchor tag instead of Link tag but react router dom says that you must use Link tag instead of anchor tag because i have to keep track of all the pages.So you have to use Link tag.Interestingly,when we see in inspect in chrome,we see that react router dom is  using anchor tag behind the scene.

import React, { useState } from 'react'
import Logo from "./Assets/Images/villa.jpeg"
import { Link } from 'react-router-dom';
const Header = () => {
  const [isLoggedIn,setisLoggedIn]=useState(false)
    return (
      <div className="header">
        <img
          src={Logo}
          style={{ width: 100, height: 50, objectFit: "contain" }}
        />
        <ul>
          <Link to={"/"}>
          <li>Home</li>
          </Link>
          <Link to={"/about"}>

          <li>About</li>
          </Link>
          <Link to={"/contact"}>

          <li>Contact</li>
          </Link>
          <li>Cart</li>
        </ul>
        {isLoggedIn?<button onClick={()=>setisLoggedIn(false)}>Logout</button>:<button  onClick={()=>setisLoggedIn(true)}>Login</button>}
      </div>
    );
  };
  export  {Header};
